{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "One entry per landscape type. Values are in a normalized 0-1 tile so they work at any size (D3, D5). recipe: 0 hills, 1 mountains, 2 dunes, 3 seabed, 4 coastal cliffs, 5 canyon, 6 mesa, 7 badlands, 8 volcanic, 9 glacial valley, 10 riverbed, 11 volcano, 12 craters. styles: optional per-type kinds (index = node Style input; look overrides type values). controls: optional per-type sliders (prop = object property, slot = node input P1-P4). height = relief as a fraction of the landscape's size. feature_scale = main shapes across the tile. sharpness > 1 = pointier tops, flatter lows. rock = real-size rock grain on steep and high ground (0 = none; sand and the Moon get none). grain_roughness = how fast rock grain fades with size (0.5 smooth .. 0.66 rubbly), from the 1 m lidar. erosion = the erosion engine's settings for this type (erosion.py; on, amount, talus_deg, soften, deposit, m). feature_label / feature_noun = what Feature Size is called for this type and what the 'about N across' readout counts. groups = display order and headers in the type picker ([key, label, [type keys]]).",
